Hello!

This is my first message to this list.  I'm interested in fixing support 
for Terratec EWS88 MT, and I think my experience with the GNU build system 
will be useful too.

That's what I'm going to start with.  The top-level "build" script on CVS 
is incomplete - it doesn't create a working build from a clean checkout.  

Explanation of the patch:

1) If EXTRA_ALSA_DRIVER_CONFIG_FLAGS is already set, it should not be
overwritten.  This would make it easy to reuse the CVS build script from
more automated scripts, instead of copying it to another location or
modifying it and losing it at the next CVS cleanup.

2) For "build prep", aclocal should be called in alsa-driver.  "make
all-deps" creates acinclude.m4, but not aclocal.m4.

3) For "build prep", libtoolize and aclocal should be called in alsa-lib.  
The project requires libtool, but ltmain.sh is (rightly) not in CVS, so it
should be copied there by running libtoolize.  aclocal should be run after
libtoolize to create aclocal.m4.

4) "alsa-utils/cvscompile" should call autoheader, just like "build" does.

Please also remove the following files from CVS:

alsa-utils/install-sh
alsa-utils/missing
alsa-utils/mkinstalldirs
alsa-utils/include/aconfig.h.in

The first three of them are installed by Automake.  Please note that the
old "missing" on ALSA CVS is incomptible with the latest _stable_ version
of Automake 1.6.3.

alsa-utils/include/aconfig.h.in is generated by autoheader, which is 
called in "build", and will be called in alsa-utils/cvscompile after 
applying this patch.

==================================
--- build
+++ build
@@ -6,7 +6,9 @@
 
 # Comment this out if you don't want isapnp support in ALSA driver RPM
 #
-export EXTRA_ALSA_DRIVER_CONFIG_FLAGS="--with-isapnp=yes --with-sequencer=yes"
+test -z $EXTRA_ALSA_DRIVER_CONFIG_FLAGS &&
+    EXTRA_ALSA_DRIVER_CONFIG_FLAGS="--with-isapnp=yes --with-sequencer=yes"
+export EXTRA_ALSA_DRIVER_CONFIG_FLAGS
 
 # All commands must succeed
 set -e
@@ -37,10 +39,13 @@
       fi
     fi
     make ALSAKERNELDIR="$ALSAKERNELDIR" all-deps
+    aclocal
     autoconf
     
     cd ../alsa-lib
     echo "Pre-configuring alsa-lib"
+    libtoolize --force
+    aclocal
     autoheader
     automake --foreign --add-missing
     autoconf
--- alsa-utils/cvscompile
+++ alsa-utils/cvscompile
@@ -1,6 +1,7 @@
 #!/bin/bash
 
 aclocal $ACLOCAL_FLAGS
+autoheader
 automake --foreign --add-missing
 autoconf
 export CFLAGS='-O2 -Wall -pipe -g'
==================================

